<article class="env-definition" id="07WP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07WP">Definition <span data-tag="07WP">98.5.1</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{Z}$ be a category fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$. We say $\mathcal{Z}$ satisfies <em>condition (RS)</em> if for every pushout </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix{ X \ar[r] \ar[d] &  X' \ar[d] \\  Y \ar[r] &  Y' = Y \amalg _ X X' }  \]
</div>
  <p> in the category of schemes over $S$ where </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$X$, $X'$, $Y$, $Y'$ are spectra of local Artinian rings, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X$, $X'$, $Y$, $Y'$ are of finite type over $S$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$X \to X'$ (and hence $Y \to Y'$) is a closed immersion 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> the functor of fibre categories </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathcal{Z}_{Y'} \longrightarrow \mathcal{Z}_ Y \times _{\mathcal{Z}_ X} \mathcal{Z}_{X'}  \]
</div>
  <p> is an equivalence of categories. </p>
</article>